## Best Practices

1. Always validate filters before Qdrant operations using `is_filter_valid_for_embedding()`
2. Check collection existence before operations using `__qdrant_collection_exits()`
3. Handle Qdrant exceptions gracefully - log errors and return empty results or appropriate status codes
4. Use submodule business objects for database operations, never SQLAlchemy directly
5. Calculate similarity thresholds when recreating collections
6. Support both record IDs and tensor IDs for embeddings with sub_keys
7. Include access control checks when access management is active
8. Use type hints for all function parameters and return types
9. Keep helper functions private (prefix with `__`)
10. Document functions with docstrings describing parameters and return values
